{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Jacob came shalem.</b> One needs to know what he intends by saying <b>shalem</b>, and our Sages of blessed memory (Shabbat 33b) offered homiletical interpretations. Further, one needs to know the intent of the verse in saying <b>when he came from Paddan-aram</b>; what is intended by this is not known. And Rashi of blessed memory explained it as ״like a person who says״ and so forth — one should examine his words; but this matter is already known from the preceding narratives." "<b>However,</b> it appears that the verse informs us that whatever our father Jacob diminished from his possessions in the gift that he gave to Esau, HaShem made up his loss from the possessions — from the possessions he brought from Paddan-aram. This is what it means by <b>And Jacob came shalem</b> etc. <b>when he came from Paddan</b> etc. — meaning, shalem in possessions as at the measure of his coming from Paddan-aram. For even though he was diminished from them by a great gift, nevertheless HaShem restored it to him; and this is the blessing of ״all״ that HaShem gave him, as I explained (Genesis 33:11)."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:48.332632827Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}